---
import Page from '../components/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---
<Page title="Privacy Policy" section="Legal" path="/privacy/" description="How Navigator Coast handles personal data: very little of it, with no accounts, no advertising trackers and no cookies."
  sources={[
    { title: 'Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (General Data Protection Regulation)', url: 'https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj' },
    { title: "UK Information Commissioner's Office: UK GDPR guidance", url: 'https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/uk-gdpr-guidance-and-resources/' },
    { title: 'Comissão Nacional de Proteção de Dados (Portugal)', url: 'https://www.cnpd.pt/' },
    { title: 'State of California, Department of Justice: California Consumer Privacy Act', url: 'https://oag.ca.gov/privacy/ccpa' },
  ]}>
  <p>This policy explains how personal data is handled when you use Navigator Coast (navigatorcoast.tourground.com). The site is built to need very little personal data: there are no accounts, no comments, no advertising trackers, no analytics scripts and no cookies.</p>
  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>The controller of personal data processed through this site is Tourground, the publisher of Navigator Coast. Contact details are at the end of this page.</p>
  <h2>What we process, why, and on what basis</h2>
  <p><strong>1. Server logs.</strong> Our hosting provider, Vercel, processes technical request data (such as IP address, time, requested address and browser details) to deliver pages and protect the service against abuse. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in operating a secure website (GDPR and UK GDPR Article 6(1)(f)).</p>
  <p><strong>2. Newsletter sign-ups.</strong> The sign-up form does not send data to us directly. It opens an email from your own mail app to {SITE.email}. If you send it, we keep your email address on our mailing list to send you the Navigator Coast letter. Legal basis: your consent (Article 6(1)(a)), which you can withdraw at any time by replying “unsubscribe” or emailing us.</p>
  <p><strong>3. Emails you send us.</strong> If you email us, we process your email address, your name if given, and your message to reply and to handle any correction request. Legal basis: legitimate interest in answering you.</p>
  <p>We do not sell personal data, share it for cross-context behavioural advertising, or use it for automated decision-making.</p>
  <h2>Who receives it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Vercel Inc.</strong> (hosting), acting as our processor.</li>
    <li><strong>Our email provider</strong>, acting as our processor, for messages you send us and for sending the newsletter.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Vercel is based in the United States. Where personal data is transferred outside the EU or the UK, we rely on the safeguards the law provides, such as an adequacy decision or standard contractual clauses.</p>
  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Server logs: for the period set by our hosting provider for security and operations.</li>
    <li>Newsletter addresses: until you unsubscribe.</li>
    <li>Emails: as long as needed to deal with your message, then for up to two years so we can show how a correction request was handled, unless the law requires longer.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p><strong>EU and UK (GDPR, UK GDPR):</strong> access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability, and objection to processing based on legitimate interests. You may complain to your data-protection authority; in Portugal that is the Comissão Nacional de Proteção de Dados (CNPD), and in the UK the Information Commissioner's Office.</p>
  <p><strong>California and other US states with privacy laws:</strong> the right to know, to delete, to correct, and to opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information. We do not sell or share personal information as those laws define it.</p>
  <p>To use any of these rights, email us. We will answer within the time the law allows (one month under the GDPR and UK GDPR, which can be extended in some cases).</p>
  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site is for adults planning travel. It is not directed at children and we do not knowingly collect their data.</p>
  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy, we update the “last reviewed” date at the top of the page.</p>
</Page>
